From ff9dec1b44ffd934ef91b472de4a43d76a0ed60a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 01:49:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Epic 7B.4: Organization Query & People Integration (ADR-012)

Exposes the Organization domain for read-side consumers and retires the
organization-reference placeholder that was wired into production with
dev-fixture-only data. No new aggregates; read-only.

- OrganizationQueryService: resolveCurrentAssignment, resolveAssignmentAsOf,
  resolveAssignmentHistory, resolveManager, resolveReports, resolveOrgPath
  (ancestor chain), resolveDescendants, resolveOrgUnitsByKind, and a
  standalone Location lookup. Composes the three existing read repositories
  only - never Prisma directly, never the write side - so every placement
  question resolves through Assignment (ADR-012 SS12 invariant #5).
- Assignment gains listCurrentByManager (+Prisma+in-memory), backed by a new
  partial index on (tenant_id, manager_id) WHERE effective_until IS NULL,
  for an efficient "direct reports" query - verified against real Postgres.
- People-facing OrganizationPlacementService (port + Prisma impl) is the one
  place an Organization id becomes a display name: composes
  OrganizationQueryService with a minimal, direct employee display-name
  lookup. Department/team are derived from the org path (the nearest
  DEPARTMENT/TEAM ancestor of the assigned OrgUnit), since OrgUnit is a
  general recursive tree, not a fixed two-level hierarchy.
- Migrated all three real consumers off the placeholder: People profile,
  People directory (row display + department picker), and the Hire flow's
  department/team/manager pickers - retiring
  organization-reference-{repository,service}.ts entirely.
- Architecture fitness: the query service can't import Prisma directly or
  the write side; client components can't import either server composition;
  a structural test confirms exactly one query service, one placement-service
  implementation, and that placement resolution never reads a denormalized
  Employee field.
- 60 new/updated unit tests + 1 new integration test (listCurrentByManager
  against real Postgres).

Known gap, documented rather than papered over: Assignment carries no
locationId (deferred in 7B.2/7B.3), so Location lookup is standalone and not
yet part of "current placement" - profile.location still reads the legacy
workLocation string. Closing that requires a future write-side slice.

